1
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:06,700
This is Trigun.

2
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:33,580
Oh, my God.

3
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:00,566
How long have you been still?

4
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,680
I've been watching you the entire time.

5
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:06,760
You are one creepy guy.

6
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:11,140
Well, I really must say, I'm
surprised you decided to appear.

7
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:14,526
Did you think it was the
idle talk of a drunk?

8
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:17,426
You can hardly blame me
if I did, now can you?

9
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:20,037
When you're stuck in a cellar like this,

10
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:22,877
with gunpowder up your
nose for over twenty years,

11
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:25,548
you stop caring whether
or not talk is true.

12
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:29,040
So tell me, who am I hunting?

13
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:37,280
Oh yeah, I can feel the shivers.

14
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:41,268
Suddenly I remember why I've
been doing this all these years.

15
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:46,140
Be sure you show our master your
gratitude for keeping you here.

16
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:49,310
Hey!

17
00:02:49,393 --> 00:02:50,740
I finally found you!

18
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:52,857
I've been looking for
you for a whole week.

19
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:55,877
I was told that you're rarely
open because you sell other stuff.

20
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,557
Well, besides boots, I mean.

21
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:58,470
Who knew?

22
00:02:58,553 --> 00:03:00,780
Hey Sonny, you sure like to talk a lot.

23
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:04,081
I hope you like to talk
about boots for your sake.

24
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,030
I do.

25
00:03:06,113 --> 00:03:07,757
But there's something else I want to know.

26
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:08,997
I'll abide by your rules.

27
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:10,037
I won't make any trouble.

28
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:11,591
Come on, what do you say?

29
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:30,857
Isn't this the most beautiful
day you've ever seen, Meryl?

30
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:32,240
Yes, it's beautiful.

31
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:34,957
It's the kind of day
that just makes you want

32
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:36,997
to sit here and forget
all about your problems.

33
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:37,997
Don't you agree?

34
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:39,060
Yes, definitely.

35
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:43,997
In fact, it makes you want to completely
forget about work and take the day off.

36
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:45,668
Not a chance, but nice try.

37
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:47,550
Shucks.

38
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:49,400
Get it over here!

39
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,080
The sky is unbelievably blue.

40
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:59,400
Hey, give me the ball!

41
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:00,700
No way!

42
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:07,500
There I go again.

43
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:09,944
Guess it's kind of stupid, huh?

44
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,717
I still keep thinking how
I'd like to show it to you,

45
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:14,817
even though that's no longer possible.

46
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,460
I just can't help myself.

47
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:23,100
Whoa, man!

48
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:24,811
I'm really, really sorry!

49
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,580
Are you okay, mister?

50
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,560
The deadly dodgeball head!

51
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:35,477
A simple technique to hold the
ball in place with intense suction!

52
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,913
Try this at home, kids!

53
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:40,260
Hey, it's Mr. Bash!

54
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:46,879
What in the hell is that man doing?

55
00:04:58,100 --> 00:04:59,629
Isn't it wonderful, Meryl?

56
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:00,790
Huh?

57
00:05:00,873 --> 00:05:03,094
That the Vash we know and love is back!

58
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:04,517
Have you gone insane?

59
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:06,188
What are you talking about?

60
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:09,257
All right, guys, who wants ice cream, huh?

61
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:10,217
Are you treating?

62
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:11,130
All right!

63
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:13,420
Get six, okay?

64
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:15,337
But why do you want six of them?

65
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:16,832
Isn't that one too many?

66
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:18,642
One is for her.

67
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,410
Here you go.

68
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:26,157
We've got a ball.

69
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:27,769
You want to come and play?

70
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,649
Wait, where are you going?

71
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:36,753
We're over here, honey.

72
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,830
We're over here.

73
00:05:37,913 --> 00:05:38,743
Here it goes!

74
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:49,380
Hey, mister! Over here! I'll get him out!

75
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:18,880
I found you, Vash the Stampede.

76
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:21,057
What?

77
00:06:21,140 --> 00:06:22,400
Who are you?

78
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:25,500
Legato.

79
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:27,780
Legato Blue Summers.

80
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,820
Mr. Vash? Hmm?

81
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:36,100
Well, uh, it's n-nothing.

82
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:37,450
Ah!

83
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,020
Hey, lady!

84
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,000
Corée! Coming!

85
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:45,180
What was that strange look on his face?

86
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:46,458
It was frightening.

87
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,571
What do you want from me?

88
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:57,000
You're alive.

89
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:02,320
Perhaps that was a bit too dramatic.

90
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:05,600
Actually, I'm here as a messenger.

91
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:07,560
That's right.

92
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:09,620
I've come here to warn you.

93
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:13,780
I'm afraid your life
is going to end today.

94
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:16,030
What?

95
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,760
Do you think I'm lying to me?

96
00:07:34,740 --> 00:07:37,540
I haven't given you a gift yet, have I?

97
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:57,400
Your reaction was better than I hoped.

98
00:07:58,100 --> 00:07:58,940
You're fun.

99
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:01,458
And to think I could kill every man,

100
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:04,637
woman, and child here in the
blink of an eye if I wanted to.

101
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:06,779
The power of death is intoxicating.

102
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:11,260
Don't be in so much of a hurry.

103
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,440
You still have a little time left.

104
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,180
Or, perhaps you don't.

105
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:20,500
And don't worry, no one
else needs to get hurt.

106
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:23,060
So do you want to draw.

107
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,480
Oh, I almost forgot.

108
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:38,644
This is a little farewell gift.

109
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:40,760
It contains a lesson from me.

110
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,612
I'll just leave it here.

111
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:46,820
Help me!

112
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:48,117
What's up with her?

113
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,157
That's a shoemaker's wife.

114
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,887
Wow, she looks really upset.

115
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:53,100
Hey! It's murder!

116
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:55,480
It's okay, calm down. Murder?

117
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:56,470
What do you mean?

118
00:08:56,553 --> 00:08:57,537
What are you talking about?

119
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,460
My husband!

120
00:08:58,620 --> 00:09:00,397
My husband's in there, but he won't talk!

121
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,774
He can't say anything!

122
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:04,297
I'm sorry, but I can't
seem to understand you!

123
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:05,968
What are you trying to say?

124
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:07,020
He won't talk!

125
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:09,080
He won't say a word!

126
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:12,210
My husband!

127
00:09:12,293 --> 00:09:13,440
My husband!

128
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:18,320
Sheriff, he didn't do it!

129
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:19,290
He's innocent!

130
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:23,077
Save it for the judge to decide,
lady, this is not a courthouse.

131
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:26,937
Listen, we have witness testimony
that places him at the shoe store.

132
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:31,657
He also just happened to be the one
closest by when the owner's body was found.

133
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:33,300
And we've got evidence.

134
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:34,830
What's more,

135
00:09:34,913 --> 00:09:36,697
we ran a check and found
out he's that humanoid

136
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:39,257
typhoon everyone's been
talking about lately.

137
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:43,017
I'd have to be completely out of
my mind not to lock up that guy.

138
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:46,577
Now, if I were to cut him loose and
he was to make off into the night,

139
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:47,717
would you take the heat?

140
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,000
I think not.

141
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:00,720
It's a little farewell gift.

142
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:02,372
I'll just leave it here.

143
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:06,800
I'm afraid your life
is going to end today.

144
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:12,160
What does he want from me?

145
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:15,200
A 60 billion double dollar reward?

146
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:16,690
No.

147
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:19,760
Is it him?

148
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:31,000
Oh, hey, Vash.

149
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:47,080
Um, Mr. Vash?

150
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,310
Oh, hi.

151
00:10:52,393 --> 00:10:53,986
Is everything all right here?

152
00:10:55,140 --> 00:10:56,340
Oh, it's just you.

153
00:10:58,140 --> 00:10:59,400
Uh-huh. Oh, Vash!

154
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:04,577
I'm so sorry about all of this, but will
you please stay here just for today?

155
00:11:04,660 --> 00:11:06,954
We'll come for you tomorrow, I promise.

156
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:08,533
That's nice, thank you.

157
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:10,937
But don't go out of
your way from me, okay?

158
00:11:11,020 --> 00:11:14,902
As far as I know, you're innocent
and haven't done anything wrong.

159
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:17,771
I need some time alone to think right now.

160
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:23,900
Um, hey, Mr. Vash? Yes?

161
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:28,100
Well, uh, actually, actually it's nothing!

162
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:32,820
What does that mean, Millie?

163
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:34,728
Actually, it means nothing!

164
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,160
What?

165
00:11:52,340 --> 00:11:53,200
What was that?

166
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:05,180
Get down!

167
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:26,460
Get down!

168
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:47,951
Thanks for showing me in.

169
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:51,900
Can you hear me, Vash the Stampede?

170
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:54,840
My name is Monev the Gale,

171
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,800
and I'm here to send you to
hell just as you were promised.

172
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,320
Both of you, run!

173
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:04,655
What's going on here?

174
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:06,557
Get out while you can!

175
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:07,470
The enemy is coming!

176
00:13:07,553 --> 00:13:08,383
Hurry!

177
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:10,245
What do you mean by the enemy?

178
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:12,458
Who is he and what is he doing here?

179
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:18,657
this was simple simple
enough to make me realize

180
00:13:18,740 --> 00:13:24,620
I've been wasting my life
let go of him right now

181
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:35,717
why do you have any idea
how long 20 years is

182
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:37,997
imprisoned in that
disgusting place with nothing

183
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:40,157
to do but physical
training it was like living

184
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:44,080
in the bowels of hell
but once I kill you those

185
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:50,417
days of torture will be over forever.

186
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:55,300
Five clicks into the end.
Four. Three. Two. One.

187
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:56,820
Why you?

188
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:09,632
It's true what I was told about this guy.

189
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:11,586
He's a complete chicken shit.

190
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,700
Uh, Mira? What are you doing?

191
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,153
We should go after him.

192
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:19,680
Uh, something's wrong with Bash.

193
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:21,630
What?

194
00:14:21,713 --> 00:14:22,543
The way he's been acting.

195
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:25,160
What? What happened?

196
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:28,297
Looks like somebody attacked
the sheriff's office.

197
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:31,717
Was it Prince of that guy in
jail trying to set him free?

198
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:32,920
Stay away from me!

199
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:34,298
Run for your lives!

200
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:35,330
Coming through!

201
00:14:35,413 --> 00:14:37,357
Whatever you do, don't get near me!

202
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,077
Take cover until I'm safely out of town!

203
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:39,997
I'm not kidding.

204
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:42,057
It's a matter of life and death here.

205
00:14:42,140 --> 00:14:43,040
It's the guy!

206
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:44,440
Vash, a stampede!

207
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:46,280
I said sit down!

208
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:51,140
I'm sorry for it!

209
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:54,670
No people!

210
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:57,797
You know that pinhead
arrogant little twerk?

211
00:14:57,880 --> 00:15:01,497
Does he actually think he can get
away from me and keep up this pace?

212
00:15:01,580 --> 00:15:02,410
Run!

213
00:15:02,493 --> 00:15:03,323
Run or I'll shoot!

214
00:15:03,406 --> 00:15:05,615
Yeah, run, hot shot, whatever you say.

215
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:07,371
You idiots, I warned you!

216
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:13,237
Still helping others
even at a time like this?

217
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:14,150
You are weak.

218
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:18,497
If you have any expectations of staying
alive, you better use them as a shield.

219
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:21,345
But don't worry, it'll
all be over soon anyway.

220
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:35,917
Now's the end of Vash the Stampede!

221
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,220
You and this town die together!

222
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:14,640
Oh, my God.

223
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,840
I did it!

224
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:42,960
I did it!

225
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:46,200
So much for the legendary
outlaw! He was nothing!

226
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:49,000
He died like a coward! At last!

227
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:50,560
At last I'm free!

228
00:16:50,940 --> 00:16:53,340
Now I can live the way I want to live!

229
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:24,840
Ah...

230
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:27,030
This...

231
00:17:27,113 --> 00:17:28,480
this must be a nightmare.

232
00:17:30,600 --> 00:17:31,580
Those eyes...

233
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:35,988
It's like looking in
the eyes of the Diablo!

234
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:51,780
He did go this way, didn't he?

235
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:53,670
Yes.

236
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:57,160
Mr. Vash!

237
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:02,640
Stay back!

238
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:05,400
Stay away from me.

239
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,020
Who is he?

240
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,580
That's not Vash.

241
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:17,151
That is not the same man.

242
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:19,980
He's walking away.

243
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:24,654
If we let him leave now, he'll
probably never come back.

244
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:27,140
I don't think we can stop him.

245
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:29,300
The way he's acting?

246
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:32,168
I don't think anyone
can stop him right now.

247
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:37,800
I can't believe the way he shot at me.

248
00:18:38,380 --> 00:18:42,197
Isn't he supposed to be so spineless
that he's unable to kill a fly?

249
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:44,045
He was like the devil himself.

250
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:46,441
He's shown his true nature to me.

251
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:49,317
But I still have to take his life.

252
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:50,860
I have no choice.

253
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,157
Wait! Wait! What do you want?

254
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:55,417
I need to use your safe.

255
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:56,330
Open it.

256
00:18:56,413 --> 00:18:59,440
But, sir, I can't... I...
I... Hurry! There's no time!

257
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:06,220
Two shots left.

258
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:08,320
How can I do this?

259
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,620
I see your plan.

260
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:14,351
You're gonna use the big safe as a shield.

261
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:16,320
I'll mutilate you!

262
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,760
Along with that vault door!

263
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:39,000
You have no more bullets, coward!

264
00:19:48,280 --> 00:19:49,640
Ah, a hidden gun.

265
00:19:49,940 --> 00:19:51,587
Why didn't he use it before?

266
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,588
He could have shot me then.

267
00:19:56,780 --> 00:19:57,640
You'll pay.

268
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,540
You will pay for this!

269
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:07,197
They're dead.

270
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,800
The people are dead.

